1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,820
You've eaten at McDonald's. But you've
never seen its biggest business:

2
00:00:04,840 --> 00:00:09,287
$10.4 billion a year, from
something you can't eat.

3
00:00:09,307 --> 00:00:14,818
It's rent. About 95% of McDonald's
restaurants are run by franchisees.

4
00:00:14,838 --> 00:00:17,714
And most of them pay rent… to McDonald's.

5
00:00:17,734 --> 00:00:21,892
In its biggest markets, McDonald's
owns the land under more than half its

6
00:00:21,912 --> 00:00:24,712
restaurants, and about
80% of the buildings.

7
00:00:24,732 --> 00:00:26,632
The royalties on all those burgers?

8
00:00:26,652 --> 00:00:32,162
About $6 billion. The rent? $10.4 billion.

9
00:00:32,182 --> 00:00:36,810
Back in the fifties, its finance chief
Harry Sonneborn put it like this:

10
00:00:36,830 --> 00:00:39,450
We are not technically
in the food business.

11
00:00:39,470 --> 00:00:41,564
We are in the real estate business.

12
00:00:41,584 --> 00:00:43,634
The burger gets you in the door.

13
00:00:43,654 --> 00:00:45,796
The door is what they own.

14
00:00:45,816 --> 00:00:48,166
Your Big Mac pays the rent.
